{"id": "EUVD-2026-97067", "enisaUuid": "a8cde144-d1b4-3292-a4e9-7cb53aeccb3b", "description": "pH7Builder (pH7 Social Dating CMS) before 18.5.0 contains an information disclosure vulnerability that allows API clients to obtain sensitive member data because UserController::users() and user() return unfiltered database rows. Attackers holding a valid private API key can retrieve bcrypt password hashes, non-expiring hashValidation reset tokens, and TOTP secrets to take over accounts and bypass two-factor authentication.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T14:58:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:58:34", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/pH7Software/pH7-Social-Dating-CMS/commit/52a59da534c7666f7607c8a9b8c42037eb4de66d", "https://github.com/pH7Software/pH7-Social-Dating-CMS/blob/v18.4.1/_protected/app/system/modules/api/controllers/UserController.php#L161-L206", "https://github.com/pH7Software/pH7-Social-Dating-CMS", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ph7builder-before-18.5.0-sensitive-data-exposure-via-member-api-usercontroller"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3m9j-mmxr-3x76", "CVE-2026-108904"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "60c7c588-be1d-3745-8d39-ea5e15a0e790", "product": {"name": "ph7builder", "vendor": {"name": "ph7software"}}, "product_version": "0 <18.5.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "06c335c8-7c64-375c-a843-197f625f968c", "vendor": {"name": "ph7software"}}], "isExploited": false}